sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"B001261","fullName":"Sen. Barrasso, John [R-WY]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WY"},{"bioguideId":"R000618","fullName":"Sen. Ricketts, Pete [R-NE]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NE"},{"bioguideId":"C001098","fullName":"Sen. Cruz, Ted [R-TX]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"L000575","fullName":"Sen. Lankford, James [R-OK]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OK"},{"bioguideId":"H001079","fullName":"Sen. Hyde-Smith, Cindy [R-MS]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MS"},{"bioguideId":"G000359","fullName":"Sen. Graham, Lindsey [R-SC]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SC"},{"bioguideId":"C001056","fullName":"Sen. Cornyn, John [R-TX]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T06:37:56+00:00","id":"s1823-119","introducedDate":"2025-05-20","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-05-20","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Environment and Public Works."},"laws":[],"number":"1823","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Agriculture and Food","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"M001190","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Mullin, Markwayne [R-OK]","party":"R","state":"OK"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-05-20","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Black Vulture Relief Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill allows livestock producers and their employees to take certain actions against black vultures to protect livestock. (Black vultures are protected under the Migratory Bird Treaty Act.)</p><p>Specifically, livestock producers and their employees may (1) take (i.e., capture, kill, or disperse, or transport the carcass of) a black vulture that they reasonably believe will cause death, injury, or destruction to livestock; or (2) in the course of taking or attempting to take the black vulture, cause injury to the bird. However, they may not take or attempt to take a black vulture through the use of poison.</p><p>Livestock producers and their employees must submit an annual report to the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service (FWS) on black vultures taken under this bill. The FWS must develop a reporting form and&nbsp;make this reporting form available on its website.</p><p>Currently, the FWS has a permit process under the Migratory Bird Treaty Act for the taking of black vultures.</p>","updateDate":"2025-06-13T10:46:01Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Black Vulture Relief Act of 2025","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-09-08T18:12:22Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-08T18:12:22Z"}
